The best hardcore RPG since Plansescape: Torment.
Let's see:
A profound story graced with political itrigue, esoteric mystery and brutal warfare;
An extremely clever and involving turn-based combat system, which rewards tactical prowess and is very well supported by the in-game gear and utility items;
Meaningful choices implemented in each and every facet of the game - character creation, dialogues, combat, quest rewards;
The epitome of replayability: each class - as well as different builds and some faction choices - feels like a whole new game;
An elegant UI, which is a pleasure to use.
The only obvious flaw here is the dated graphics/animations but you will be too busy with your questing and fighting to stop and frown at some market slave's robot-like postures.
9/10

